description:
At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth &nbsp;opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

As a&nbsp; Stations &amp;&nbsp; Authorizations &nbsp; Manager , you will play a key role in&nbsp; establishing &nbsp;and expanding Flix’s station and terminal network in Peru. Working closely with the&nbsp; local&nbsp; Sales Manager and cross-functional teams, you will take ownership of the station strategy, build relationships with key stakeholders, secure access to existing infrastructure, and develop alternative solutions where existing terminals are not available. &nbsp;

This is a highly hands-on role combining strategic thinking with extensive field work. You will&nbsp; be responsible for &nbsp;turning the station strategy into concrete actions, developing long-lasting relationships across the terminal and transportation industry, and ensuring that our stations provide a safe, attractive, and reliable experience for our passengers.

In parallel,&nbsp; you take ownership of the authorization process and ensure that our applications are&nbsp; submitted &nbsp;correctly and&nbsp; in a timely manner ,&nbsp; in accordance with &nbsp;Peruvian legislation. &nbsp;

About the Role

• Work directly with the Sales Manager to define, structure, and deliver key strategic projects related to stations and infrastructure. &nbsp;

• Take ownership of Flix’s station and terminal strategy across Peru, translating strategic&nbsp; objectives &nbsp;into concrete actions and results. &nbsp;

• Build and&nbsp; maintain &nbsp;long-lasting relationships with key stakeholders in the bus station, terminal, transportation, and infrastructure industries. &nbsp;

• Identify &nbsp;and secure access to the best sales and customer points within existing infrastructure across Peru. &nbsp;

• Develop and implement alternative station strategies in cities where access to existing terminals or infrastructure is limited. &nbsp;

• Explore opportunities to develop or establish Flix’s own station infrastructure where existing solutions are not available. &nbsp;

• Continuously evaluate and&nbsp; optimize &nbsp;Flix’s station and terminal strategy based on business needs, customer experience, operational requirements, and market opportunities. &nbsp;

• Work closely with Operations and Public Affairs teams throughout the application and authorization processes for stations and terminals. &nbsp;

• Take ownership of the authorization process, ensuring that required permits, documentation, and approvals are managed efficiently and on time. &nbsp;

• Identify &nbsp;opportunities to simplify, standardize, and continuously improve the authorization process as the business scales. &nbsp;

• Build relationships with municipalities and other relevant authorities to communicate Flix’s objectives and develop support for our operations in Peru. &nbsp;

• Represent Flix at industry networking events and actively develop a strong network of relevant contacts across the transportation and infrastructure ecosystem. &nbsp;

• Ensure that stations and terminals provide a safe, attractive, and customer-friendly environment for Flix passengers. &nbsp;

• Work closely with internal stakeholders to ensure station solutions are aligned with commercial, operational, legal, and customer requirements. &nbsp;

• Spend&nbsp; significant time &nbsp;in the field, visiting terminals, meeting stakeholders, assessing infrastructure, and developing new opportunities. &nbsp;

About You

• 5+ years of professional experience in transportation, infrastructure, terminals, stations, concessions, public affairs, commercial development, or&nbsp; a related &nbsp;field. &nbsp;

• Proven experience working directly with bus terminals, transportation infrastructure,&nbsp; authorizations , or similar physical infrastructure. &nbsp;

